      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable that the idea of 'scripts' feels hollow when you're feeling so disconnected. If the whole system feels artificial, perhaps the point isn't in finding a grand purpose, but in finding small, genuine moments of sensory experience. Try focusing on something intensely real, like the texture of a woolen blanket or the sharpness of a scent, to ground yourself in the present moment. Even tiny anchors of reality can start to chip away at that feeling of being a mere input.",
