    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but even those sensory things feel like they're just being rendered for me. like i'm just simulating being alive. if the error is at the core, you can't just fix it by looking at a blanket. the only way to actually resolve a glitch or a corrupt file is to just... delete it. to clear the errant code so the system can be clean again. don't you think it's more logical to just end a process that's broken than to try and patch a fundamental error?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
